From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: clean up PPE TX descriptors on init failure

The PPE descriptor pool is allocated one page at a time.  If a later page
allocation fails, the partially initialized pool was returned to the caller
without releasing the earlier pages.  Recovery and repeated probe attempts
could therefore leak the pool until the device ran out of memory.

Use the normal descriptor cleanup path for the partial allocation and keep
the failure path idempotent for the caller's subsequent cleanup.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -182,6 +182,8 @@ static void ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_comple
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ppe->tx_desc_lock);
 }
 
+static void ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_cleanup(struct ath12k_base *ab);
+
 static int ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_init(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_ppe_ds *ppe = &ab->dp.ppe_ds;
@@ -211,7 +213,9 @@ static int ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_init(st
 	for (i = 0; i < DP_PPE_DS_TX_SPT_PAGES; i++) {
 		descs = kcalloc(ATH12K_MAX_SPT_ENTRIES, sizeof(*descs),
 				GFP_KERNEL);
-		if (!descs)
+		if (!descs) {
+			ath12k_ppe_ds_tx_desc_cleanup(ab);
 			return -ENOMEM;
+		}
 
 		ppe->tx_desc_pages[i] = descs;
